      "writtenOn": "2023-11-27T17:56:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh, interesting. This is only ever called from C code. And the C code can\u0027t allocated memory, and AFAICT only calls this function on individual arrays on the stack, which I guess is ok. (I\u0027m pretty sure C doesn\u0027t guarantee stack layout, so trying to do multiple buffers in one go would be UB there too.)\n\n\u003e  make a flushed_zeroize_raw to be implemented in terms of a pointer and length, and make flushed_zeroize used elsewhere just a safe adapter onto that function\n\nBut TBH I think I like that more; the underlying code is using raw addresses so that shouldn\u0027t be a problem.",
